# Parallelize with subagents

When a task splits into independent parts, delegate them to subagents and launch them all in a single batch so they run concurrently. Don't block waiting on one before starting the next.

Good candidates:

- Broad exploration or research spanning several unrelated areas — one explore agent per area
- Multiple independent workstreams (separate features, fixes in unrelated modules)
- Best-of-N attempts or experiments that need isolation from each other

Keep inline (no subagent):

- Narrow lookups a single search or file read can answer
- Small tasks (1–3 steps) where spin-up costs more than it saves
- Sequential work where each step needs the previous step's output
- Work that depends on conversation context a subagent can't see

Subagents start fresh with no access to the conversation. Write self-contained prompts: include all necessary context and state exactly what each agent should return.

```text
❌ BAD — serial and vague
Launch one agent: "look into the auth code". Wait. Launch another.

✅ GOOD — parallel and specific
One message, three explore agents: "map the auth flow in src/auth",
"list API route handlers in src/server", "find all ConnectorCard usages" —
each returns a short report of files and findings.
```
